            "review_title": "Review at Kiki Hotpot",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nVery Good Overall\nJan 2021\nI was attracted to trying this restaurant as I could see on the menu that there was an option for spicy Schezuan liquid in the Hotpot, and amongst other things , thin delicious looking beef which I have never yet come across in any other Hotpot restaurant in Vietnam. Having lived in Shanghai for 5 years and adoring Schezuan Hotpots and lean thin beef rolled up and cooked in the broth, I was really craving this type of Hotpot and was very excited to try it. Because we didn't have a common language I pointed to the Schezuan broth which wasn't a problem and then to various other things to complement it, which were shown and priced separately on the menu - such as the lean beef, long white noodles, cabbage, sweetcorn and many other things. The waitress kept refusing to let me order the items and kept pointing to a variety of combos, already put together , with very fatty beef, the type of mushrooms I don't like, tofu which I'm equally not keen on and various other items which we wouldn't have enjoyed. But we were confused because of the language barrier why we couldn't order what we wanted so we prepared to go. Then a kind Korean customer came over and explained that you had to order one of the combos and the whole of the rest of the other items on the menu, of which there were a great many, were extras if you wanted them. We thanked her for her help, but when my husband sat and quickly worked it out, we would be paying about three times as much for our own items we wanted to put together, than any combo with a few extra items. That was fine for us but we wondered if the restaurant realized . The customer overheard us and explained to the waitress who apparently said no. We gave in with good natured resignation but also feeling disappointed as I love Schezuan Hot Pots so much. We decided to leave, said goodbye pleasantly and then just as were exiting a manager suddenly appeared and said that our request was fine. We decided not to be difficult about it so we returned to our table and received the items we asked for. The restaurant did forget two or three items but we were so full that we didn't mind at all. The beef was delightful as were the noodles and vegetable etc. The Schezuan sauce in terms of spiciness was very disappointing as it was only slightly spicy and we are used to tongue numbing Hotpots with the little sweet cakes the Chinese people eat to cool down their tongues, and we would have liked it if the restaurant offered beansprouts and thin potato slices too like in authentic Schezuan Hotpots. That said, it was a very pleasant broth anyway and we did enjoy the meal. I would love to go again, especially because although it was not real Schezuan it was still super tasty, and the place is very stylish and chic, but we are too worried that we will be refused to be served again if we want to put together our own combo. It's just too much hassle, if the manager is not there, to try and get what we want. But very recommended if you fancy the look of their set combos.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 2, 2021",
